```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__company_tools_list","description":"List the match's Company Tools (the customer's internal systems for this match: logs, tickets, docs, ...). Their information is authoritative. Needs the START_GAME descriptor.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__company_tools_list(args: {}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__configure_session","description":"Load the machine-provided descriptor(s). Pass every lifecycle descriptor of this match in order (PREPARE_GAME then START_GAME, or RESUME_*), each as the exact JSON object or the raw frame text. Credentials stay in helper memory; the result never echoes them. Call again after every new frame.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__configure_session(args: { descriptors: Array<unknown>; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__get_backlog_item","description":"Full JSON of one visible backlog item (brief, acceptance criteria, deadline, points, statuses).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__get_backlog_item(args: {
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  key: string;
  refresh?: boolean;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__login_match","description":"Log in to the Game Master portal with the descriptor account (cookie kept in memory).

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__login_match(args: {}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__refresh_match","description":"Read /match/<matchId>: match status and clock, team, Start/Submit endpoints and every visible backlog item. During the game it logs DISCOVERED for new items. Long fields are shortened; use get_backlog_item for the full brief.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__refresh_match(args: {}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__report_progress","description":"Append one progress event (without schemaVersion/playerSessionId; they are added). Types: PREPARATION_STATUS, ENVIRONMENT_READY, GAME_START_STATUS, BACKLOG_STATUS, BACKLOG_TESTS, BLOCKER_OPENED, BLOCKER_RESOLVED, ORCHESTRATOR_RESTARTED, ORCHESTRATOR_ENDED, MODEL_USAGE. Invalid events are rejected with the reason.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__report_progress(args: { event: { [key: string]: unknown; }; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__start_work","description":"Start Work for one OPEN item (required before editing and before submit). Returns startInstruction, submitTemplate and MVS; creates <matchRoot>/answers/<ID>/submit.json from the template and the evidence/ folder; logs IN_PROGRESS. Calling again for a started item is a harmless replay.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__start_work(args: {
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  backlogItemKey: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__submit_work","description":"Submit one started item ONCE. Commit source + answers/<ID>/submit.json + evidence first and push to the assigned branch. The helper verifies the pushed revision contains the answer and every evidence/<file> it references, sends the committed answer with gitRevision and an idempotency key, retries safely, and logs SUBMITTED with the receipt.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__submit_work(args: {
  // Backlog ID shown on /match, e.g. TASK-01, CR-02, BUG-01, PI-01.
  backlogItemKey: string;
  // Full SHA; defaults to HEAD of checkoutRoot.
  gitRevision?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"},{"name":"mcp__mtm_helper__wait_for_update","description":"Block up to timeoutMs (max 55000) until the match changes (new item, status/score change, pause/end). Returns {changed, reason, board}. Call repeatedly while idle; an empty backlog is never the end of the match.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__mtm_helper__wait_for_update(args: { timeoutMs?: number; }): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```"}]

