      "title": "Paid amount and outstanding (receivable) balance of an invoice",
      "body": "paid = the sum of all payments linked to the invoice (an invoice can have several partial payments).\n\nOnly issued, unsettled invoices are receivables:\n- SENT, PARTIAL, OVERDUE: outstanding = total - paid, never below 0.\n- PAID: outstanding = 0.\n- DRAFT: not issued yet, nothing is owed: outstanding = 0.\n- VOID: cancelled, nothing is owed: outstanding = 0.\nThis is the same rule as the Finance tab of a company. Reports and exports must not show a balance for draft or void invoices, otherwise the accountant books receivables that do not exist."
    },
    {
      "id": "KB-FIN-01",
      "title": "Currency minor units and amount formatting",
      "body": "Solova stores every amount as an integer number of minor units (column suffix *Minor). Whenever an amount leaves the system (exports, reports, integrations) it is written in major units with exactly the currency's number of minor digits:\n- 2 digits: USD, EUR, GBP, AUD, CAD, SGD (12345 minor = 123.45; 10000 minor = 100.00).\n- 0 digits: VND, JPY, KRW (12345 minor = 12345).\nRules: '.' is the decimal point; no currency symbol; no thousands separator; no exponent; negative amounts use a leading '-'. Always keep the trailing zeros (100.00, not 100). Convert with integer arithmetic or the currency factor; never format with the base currency of the workspace when the invoice has its own currency."
    },
    {
      "id": "KB-SEC-01",
      "title": "Access to client financial data",
      "body": "Invoice, payment and company financial data may only be read by signed-in staff. Any new screen, endpoint or export that exposes this data must refuse anonymous requests (respond 401/403 or redirect to the login page) and must not include data in the refused response. Do not place exports in public folders or shareable links."
    }
  ]
}","structuredContent":null}

